From: Celestials316 <240407887+Celestials316@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 00:40:02 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] deps,v8: skip the cache-line layout assert on 32-bit hosts

The Node 27 alpha compiles its 32-bit host tools against a standard
library that does not provide the C++17 cache-line interference constant.
Guard V8's compile-time layout sanity check with the feature macro. The
check has no effect on object layout or runtime behavior, and it remains
enabled wherever the constant exists.
---
 deps/v8/src/heap/mutable-page.cc | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/deps/v8/src/heap/mutable-page.cc b/deps/v8/src/heap/mutable-page.cc
index a63309718d..8c7eb3693a 100644
--- a/deps/v8/src/heap/mutable-page.cc
+++ b/deps/v8/src/heap/mutable-page.cc
@@ -49,9 +49,11 @@ MutablePage::MutablePage(Heap* heap, BaseSpace* space, size_t chunk_size,
   // This assert is merely necessary but not sufficient to guarantee that the
   // fields sit on the same cacheline as the metadata object itself is
   // dynamically allocated without alignment restrictions.
+#if defined(__cpp_lib_hardware_interference_size)
   static_assert(
       kOffsetOfFirstFastField / std::hardware_destructive_interference_size ==
       kOffsetOfLastFastField / std::hardware_destructive_interference_size);
+#endif
 }
 
 // static
